### commercetools Connect release runbook
### Documentation:
### https://docs.commercetools.com/connect/getting-started#update-your-connector
###
### Run one request at a time. Do not use "Run All".
### Every update uses optimistic locking. Before each mutation, run the GET request
### immediately above it and copy the returned version into http-client.env.json.
###
### Keep secrets and project-specific values in the ignored http-client.env.json file:
### BASIC_AUTH_TOKEN                     Base64-encoded clientId:clientSecret
### BEARER_TOKEN                         OAuth access token returned below
### PROJECT_KEY                          Primary commercetools Project key
### RELEWISE_STORE_KEY                   Store to synchronize
### RELEWISE_DATASET_ID                  Relewise dataset ID
### RELEWISE_API_KEY                     Relewise API key
### RELEWISE_SERVER_URL                  Relewise server URL
### CONNECTOR_VERSION_FOR_TAG_UPDATE     Version returned before setRepository
### CONNECTOR_VERSION_FOR_PREVIEW        Version returned before updatePreviewable
### CONNECTOR_VERSION_FOR_DEPLOYMENT     Version accepted for preview deployment
### CONNECTOR_VERSION_FOR_CERTIFICATION  Version returned before certification
### PREVIEW_DEPLOYMENT_KEY               Unique key, for example relewise-0-1-0-preview
### EXISTING_DEPLOYMENT_KEY              Existing installation key, when upgrading one
### EXISTING_DEPLOYMENT_VERSION          Version returned for that installation
###
### The API Client used here needs manage_connectors and manage_connectors_deployments
### for PROJECT_KEY (or the broader manage_project scope). Preview/deployment requests
### also need manage_api_clients because connect.yaml asks Connect to generate the
### runtime API Client.

@CONNECT_REGION = europe-west1.gcp
@CONNECTOR_KEY = relewise
@RELEASE_TAG = 0.1.0
@REPOSITORY_URL = https://github.com/Relewise/relewise-integrations-commercetools-connect.git

### 1. Create a bearer token
POST https://auth.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/oauth/token
Authorization: Basic {{BASIC_AUTH_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials

### Copy access_token from the response to BEARER_TOKEN in http-client.env.json.

### 2. Read the existing ConnectorStaged before updating its Git tag
GET https://connect.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/connectors/drafts/key={{CONNECTOR_KEY}}
Authorization: Bearer {{BEARER_TOKEN}}

### Copy the returned version to CONNECTOR_VERSION_FOR_TAG_UPDATE.

### 3. Point the existing ConnectorStaged to release 0.1.0
POST https://connect.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/connectors/drafts/key={{CONNECTOR_KEY}}
Authorization: Bearer {{BEARER_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": {{CONNECTOR_VERSION_FOR_TAG_UPDATE}},
  "actions": [
    {
      "action": "setRepository",
      "url": "{{REPOSITORY_URL}}",
      "tag": "{{RELEASE_TAG}}"
    }
  ]
}

### 4. Read the updated ConnectorStaged before requesting preview validation
GET https://connect.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/connectors/drafts/key={{CONNECTOR_KEY}}
Authorization: Bearer {{BEARER_TOKEN}}

### Confirm repository.tag is 0.1.0 and copy version to CONNECTOR_VERSION_FOR_PREVIEW.

### 5. Request preview validation
POST https://connect.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/connectors/drafts/key={{CONNECTOR_KEY}}
Authorization: Bearer {{BEARER_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": {{CONNECTOR_VERSION_FOR_PREVIEW}},
  "actions": [
    {
      "action": "updatePreviewable"
    }
  ]
}

### 6. Monitor preview validation
GET https://connect.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/connectors/drafts/key={{CONNECTOR_KEY}}
Authorization: Bearer {{BEARER_TOKEN}}

### Continue only when isPreviewable is true and previewableReport has no errors.
### Copy the accepted ConnectorStaged version to CONNECTOR_VERSION_FOR_DEPLOYMENT.

### 7. Create a preview deployment
POST https://connect.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/{{PROJECT_KEY}}/deployments
Authorization: Bearer {{BEARER_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "{{PREVIEW_DEPLOYMENT_KEY}}",
  "type": "preview",
  "connector": {
    "key": "{{CONNECTOR_KEY}}",
    "version": {{CONNECTOR_VERSION_FOR_DEPLOYMENT}},
    "staged": true
  },
  "region": "{{CONNECT_REGION}}",
  "configurations": [
    {
      "applicationName": "full-sync",
      "securedConfiguration": [
        {
          "key": "RELEWISE_STORE_KEY",
          "value": "{{RELEWISE_STORE_KEY}}"
        },
        {
          "key": "RELEWISE_DATASET_ID",
          "value": "{{RELEWISE_DATASET_ID}}"
        },
        {
          "key": "RELEWISE_API_KEY",
          "value": "{{RELEWISE_API_KEY}}"
        },
        {
          "key": "RELEWISE_SERVER_URL",
          "value": "{{RELEWISE_SERVER_URL}}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

### 8. Monitor the preview deployment
GET https://connect.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/{{PROJECT_KEY}}/deployments/key={{PREVIEW_DEPLOYMENT_KEY}}
Authorization: Bearer {{BEARER_TOKEN}}

### Continue only when status is Deployed and the build report has no errors.
### Verify that a full synchronization completes and inspect its application logs.

### 9. Inspect preview application logs
GET https://connect.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/{{PROJECT_KEY}}/deployments/key={{PREVIEW_DEPLOYMENT_KEY}}/logs?applicationName=full-sync
Authorization: Bearer {{BEARER_TOKEN}}

### Marketplace certification
### Do not continue until the preview sync succeeds and the public documentation is live.

### 10. Read the ConnectorStaged before submitting it for re-certification
GET https://connect.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/connectors/drafts/key={{CONNECTOR_KEY}}
Authorization: Bearer {{BEARER_TOKEN}}

### Confirm repository.tag is 0.1.0 and copy version to CONNECTOR_VERSION_FOR_CERTIFICATION.

### 11. Submit the updated ConnectorStaged for Marketplace re-certification
POST https://connect.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/connectors/drafts/key={{CONNECTOR_KEY}}
Authorization: Bearer {{BEARER_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": {{CONNECTOR_VERSION_FOR_CERTIFICATION}},
  "actions": [
    {
      "action": "publish",
      "certification": true
    }
  ]
}

### 12. Monitor certification status, publishingReport, and certificationInfo
GET https://connect.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/connectors/drafts/key={{CONNECTOR_KEY}}
Authorization: Bearer {{BEARER_TOKEN}}

### Existing installation migration
### Run this only for a known installation after the updated Connector is published.

### 13. Read the existing installation
GET https://connect.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/{{PROJECT_KEY}}/deployments/key={{EXISTING_DEPLOYMENT_KEY}}
Authorization: Bearer {{BEARER_TOKEN}}

### Copy the returned version to EXISTING_DEPLOYMENT_VERSION.

### 14. Redeploy the installation with the latest Connector and current configuration
POST https://connect.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/{{PROJECT_KEY}}/deployments/key={{EXISTING_DEPLOYMENT_KEY}}
Authorization: Bearer {{BEARER_TOKEN}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": {{EXISTING_DEPLOYMENT_VERSION}},
  "actions": [
    {
      "action": "redeploy",
      "updateConnector": true,
      "configurationValues": [
        {
          "applicationName": "full-sync",
          "securedConfiguration": [
            {
              "key": "RELEWISE_STORE_KEY",
              "value": "{{RELEWISE_STORE_KEY}}"
            },
            {
              "key": "RELEWISE_DATASET_ID",
              "value": "{{RELEWISE_DATASET_ID}}"
            },
            {
              "key": "RELEWISE_API_KEY",
              "value": "{{RELEWISE_API_KEY}}"
            },
            {
              "key": "RELEWISE_SERVER_URL",
              "value": "{{RELEWISE_SERVER_URL}}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

### 15. Monitor the upgraded installation
GET https://connect.{{CONNECT_REGION}}.commercetools.com/{{PROJECT_KEY}}/deployments/key={{EXISTING_DEPLOYMENT_KEY}}
Authorization: Bearer {{BEARER_TOKEN}}
